  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Tarocchi Bolognesi. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Tarocchi Bolognesi (or Tarocchino Bolognese) refers to the family of games played with the specific 62-card Tarot deck from Bologna. The most common variant is Ottocento, but the term covers the deck and system itself. The deck removes ranks 2-5 from each suit of a standard Tarot pack.',
    objective: 'In the main variant Ottocento, the objective is to score points from card values and declared combinations; the first partnership to reach 800 points wins the rubber. Other variants (e.g. Terziglio, Millone) have their own targets.',
    gameplay: 'General mechanics: Must follow suit. Trumps win. Matto is an Excuse. High trumps (Angel, World, BÃ©gato) and Moors (1-4) have special status.',
